From 9e8267867e115eddc2b9e5401cdd1c936b501eb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:41:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [AGS] cc_instance.cpp: fix local int/int32_t mismatch,
 new divergence site

Another new call-site instance of the established DJGPP int32_t-vs-int
divergence category (patches 0013/0018/0019/0024's own category, not a
new mechanism): ccInstance::CallScriptFunction() declared two local
stack variables `int start_at, export_args;`, then passed them by
reference to FindExportedFunction(const String&, int32_t&, int32_t&) --
DJGPP's int32_t is `long int`, a distinct type from `int` even though
both are 4 bytes here, so an int lvalue cannot bind to an int32_t&
parameter at all (unlike the pointer-shaped instances of this same
category, a reference binding has no reinterpret_cast escape hatch
worth using here). Fixed by declaring the locals as int32_t directly,
matching FindExportedFunction's own already-correct signature -- the
callee was right, the caller's locals were wrong.

This single change also fixes a second, related error at the same call
site's own next line: `numargs = std::min(numargs, export_args);` failed
the same single-template-parameter deduction mismatch already seen in
patch 0024's room.cpp fix (numargs is the function's own int32_t
parameter; export_args was the mismatched int local) -- once
export_args is int32_t, both arguments deduce to the same real type and
std::min resolves without any further change needed.

Checked every other use of start_at/export_args in this function for a
lingering int-specific dependency before landing: export_args feeds a
cc_error() printf-style call with %d (a pre-existing latent width
mismatch on this platform independent of this patch -- int32_t is long
int here, %d expects int -- but compiles without even a -Wformat
warning in practice and is not part of this patch's scope); start_at
feeds Run(int32_t curpc) directly, now an exact type match rather than
an implicit int->int32_t conversion.

Verified: cc_instance.cpp.obj compiles clean, zero errors, zero
warnings (including no new format-string warnings from the cc_error
call). Full cmake --build ... -- -k (keep-going) re-run: no new errors
from this file, and no other error anywhere in the entire build except
the two already-documented, deliberately-deferred items -- the
ali3dsw.cpp window-surface rewrite and the remaining small rename-only
sites (debug.cpp, graphics_mode.cpp, agsplatformdriver.cpp).
---
 Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp b/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp
index dae84de91..3e88d7e29 100644
--- a/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp
+++ b/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp
@@ -394,7 +394,7 @@ ccInstError ccInstance::CallScriptFunction(const String &funcname, int32_t numar
         return kInstErr_Busy;
     }
 
-    int start_at, export_args;
+    int32_t start_at, export_args;
     if (!FindExportedFunction(funcname, start_at, export_args))
     {
         cc_error("function '%s' not found", funcname.GetCStr());
